      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(telemetry): record session.ended trajectory event after flush, not inline with model.completed",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #102014 — the `session.ended` trajectory event timestamp equals the last\n`model.completed` timestamp, making it impossible to measure actual session\nduration vs model compute time.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`session.ended` was recorded inside the try block immediately after\n`model.completed` in the same synchronous execution. Both events called\n`new Date().toISOString()` within the same millisecond, producing identical\ntimestamps.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. Defer `session.ended` from the try block to the finally block\n2. Record `session.ended` **before** `flushEmbeddedAttemptTrajectoryRecorder`\n   so the final event is included in the drained batch\n3. Capture `attemptTrajectoryTerminal.status` alongside `terminalError` and\n   use the resolved status (success/error/interrupted) instead of the generic\n   cleanup/interrupted/error fallback\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real Behavior Proof\n\nTrajectory export from a live agent session on this branch:\n\n```\nsession.started     ts=2026-07-08T06:32:15.759Z  seq=1\nmodel.completed     ts=2026-07-08T06:32:22.698Z  seq=5\nsession.ended       ts=2026-07-08T06:32:22.717Z  seq=7\n```\n\n`session.ended` (22.717, seq=7) is recorded 19ms after `model.completed`\n(22.698, seq=5), proving the event is now independent instead of inline.\n\n### Autoreview (claude-sonnet-5)\n\n```\nautoreview --mode branch --engine claude --model claude-sonnet-5\n→ patch is correct (0.95), no accepted/actionable findings\n```\n\n- [x] `oxfmt --check` passes\n- [x] `oxlint` passes\n- [x] `git diff --check` passes\n- [x] autoreview clean (claude-sonnet-5, 0.95)",
        "branch": "fix/102014-session-ended-ts",
